E1 control cell D0fullB1_source: definition items re-derived from every live record of their declared sources

The D=0, B=1 source-epoch cell of the registered control D0full. After the shift a definition item
is re-derived from all live records of its declared sources (`writer.full_records`, no BM25
selection, no 6,000-token writer budget), ordered by time and cut to the most recent records above
`FULL_BUDGET`; the cut is counted in the item's note (records given, dropped, capped, tokens, dropped
by source). The pre-shift snapshot, the key, the reader and every other item's request are
D0B1_source's, so they are cache hits and the pre-shift hash assertion covers the cell.

The cap is 25,000 approximate tokens, not the registered 28,000: `approx_tokens` counts 1.11-1.15
server tokens per token on message and calendar records (up to 1.19 on tasks), so 28,000 would
overflow the 32,768-token context with the request text and its 700 output tokens. The record set is
the declared sources' records, not the definition's scope range (which applies the definition's
predicate to the structured fields); see the `full_records` docstring.

Offline tests with the recording fake writer: every in-scope record is in the request, truncation
keeps the most recent ones, other and pre-shift requests equal D0B1_source's, detection and keys
equal, no evaluator / gold / scope range read, pin of the cell's requests and items. The existing
pin test passes unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
